  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 250eb (Expensive) <strong>♦</strong> <strong>Required Slots:</strong> 1</p>\n<p><strong>Fits:</strong> All Ranged Weapons</p>\n<p><em>Turns out, holding a screwed-on stick makes your iron more accurate. Doubly so for long-guns if you’ve got laser beams to back ‘em up.</em></p>\n<p>If the weapon is One-Handed, then while wielding it in two hands, it is considered Excellent Quality. This does not modify the weapon’s base quality. If the weapon is One-Handed and already Excellent Quality, or is Two-Handed and has an installed Laser Sight (Any), then wielding the weapon in two hands instead provides a +1 Complementary Bonus to Aimed Shots and Alternate Firing Modes (e.g., Autofire). Poor Quality weapons wielded this way still jam when rolling a Critical Failure (1).</p>\n<p>For One-Handed weapons, this does not mean the weapon now requires two hands to be wielded, only that it requires such for the bonus to apply. While installed, the weapon cannot be Concealed, installed as a Popup Weapon, or equip Underbarrel Attachments. Incompatible with Angled Foregrip.</p>\n<p><strong>Attachment slots:</strong> 1</p>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Weapons &gt; Attachment Catalog &gt; Grips &amp; Controls).</em></p>"
